.TH HOSTNAME 5
.SH NAME
hostname, motd \- the machine's name and the welcome message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/hostname
.br
.B /etc/motd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
.B /etc/hostname
the machine's name, on the first line (at most 31 characters; "sieos" when
the file is missing).
The login prompt and the shell's prompt
.RB ( user@host:dir$ )
show it;
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
puts it in a new key's comment (user@host), and
.BR git (1)
in the default author's address.
.TP
.B /etc/motd
the message of the day: shown by a login shell
.RB ( "sh \-l" )
when a session starts, before the first prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
echo laptop > /etc/hostname
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR login (8)
